                                "sense_id": "ffd9ef6c-4350-3b84-93ce-dc006ba6ef81",
                                "text": "It is still more remarkable that the reeves also, even in the presence of the males, will court each other and have intercourse. We may associate this with the high erotic development of birds, the difficulty with which tumescence seems to occur in them, and their long courtships."
